    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n80979" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περ-άσιμος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾱ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περάω</span> A) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that may be crossed,
			passable</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀὴρ ἀετῷ π</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				1047
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποταμοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arr.
					<u>An.</u>
					5.9.4
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Scymn.
				818
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				7.4.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾗ μάλιστα π. ἦν [τὸ ῥεῦμα]</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Luc.</u>
					27
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαλάσσας . . π. μόχθον</span> the
			labour <i>of crossing</i> the sea, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hymn.Is.</u>
				35
			</span></i>.</div>
